{
  "description": "Frozen test vectors for the message@1 fingerprint and canonical keys (platform/contracts/src/activity-message.ts). A collector in any language can check its own normalisation against these. fp = first 32 hex of sha256(JSON array [normalised sender, normalised text]); the fp: key = first 40 hex of sha256(JSON array [normalised sender, sent time floored to the UTC minute as ISO 8601 with milliseconds and Z, normalised text]). Normalising: Unicode NFKC, lower-case, zero-width (U+200B to U+200D, U+2060) and BOM (U+FEFF) removed, every run of whitespace one space, trimmed; text is cut to its first 8192 code points. Serialisation: the hashed array is JSON.stringify of the array, that is compact (no spaces after , or :), non-ASCII characters written as themselves in UTF-8 (never \\uXXXX escapes, so Python needs ensure_ascii=False and separators (',', ':')), and only the characters JSON requires escaped. A row may give its text as text_repeat [unit, count]; a null fp means no fingerprint. Changing any value here is a breaking change to every stored fingerprint.",
